# NEWS

## Unreleased (2026-10)

- Dictionaries are generated and one entry per line; every `der_*` symbol is documented in the
  `.dix` header; per-source provenance and licensing are in `PROVENANCE.md`.
- Regression suite (`make test`, apertium-regtest): 207 Ido→Esperanto and 205 Esperanto→Ido
  sentences.
- Generated constraint grammars for both directions, explicit epo→ido choice among Ido
  synonyms, closed-class and possessive fixes (`mia`→`mea`, `ca`→`ĉi tiu`), duration
  accusative after intransitive verbs, `tiel`→`tante`.
- The `l'` and `#`-stripping `sed` steps were removed from the ido→epo mode.

## Version 0.1.0 (2025-01-26)

### New Features
- Initial release of Apertium Ido-Esperanto translation pair
- Support for basic Ido to Esperanto translation
- Number handling in translation pipeline
- Bilingual dictionary with core vocabulary

### Technical Details
- Morphological analysis and generation
- Transfer rules for structural translation
- Post-generation rules for both languages
